{"Contextual logger middleware dereferences request fields without nil checks, causing potential panics on malformed or test-generated requests with nil req when accessing req.PluginContext": 0.749343991279602, "Logger middleware ordering issue: NewLoggerMiddleware runs before NewContextualLoggerMiddleware, causing backend request logs to lose pluginId, endpoint, datasource, and user attributes because context is not yet enriched": 0.18724006414413452, "Logger interface breaking change: Adding FromContext method and changing variadic logging methods from ...interface{} to ...any breaks out-of-tree implementations of pkg/plugins/log.Logger": 0.572452962398529, "Logger.FromContext silently drops contextual attributes for custom logger implementations because grafanaInfraLogWrapper.FromContext only handles *log.ConcreteLogger and falls back to d.New() for other types": 0.43876898288726807, "LoggerMiddleware's reliance on m.logger.FromContext(ctx) can lose existing contextual fields when grafanaInfraLogWrapper.FromContext falls back to a fresh/base logger for non-ConcreteLogger types": 0.34185388684272766, "Test logger FromContext returns NewTestLogger() unconditionally instead of preserving existing test logger state, potentially hiding contextual-logging regressions in tests": 0.524469256401062}